      "problem": "Express $\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,$ without radicals in the denominator.",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{x-1}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{x-1}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x-1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}\\cdot \\sqrt{x-1}}{(\\sqrt{x-1})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{(x+1)(x-1)}}{x-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
